{"step_index":1689,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:01:24Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport pulp\n\ndef rdn(G):\n    prob = pulp.LpProblem('RDN', pulp.LpMinimize)\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    x = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'x_{v}', cat='Binary') for v in nodes}\n    y = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'y_{v}', cat='Binary') for v in nodes}\n    prob += pulp.lpSum([x[v] + 2*y[v] for v in nodes])\n    for v in nodes:\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] <= 1\n        # v dominated: either x[v]==1, y[v]==1, or neighbor has y[u]==1\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] + pulp.lpSum([y[u] for u in G.neighbors(v)]) >= 1\n    prob.solve(pulp.PULP_CBC_CMD(msg=0))\n    return int(round(pulp.value(prob.objective)))\n\n# Check all trees up to n=15\nimport itertools\n\nfor n in range(8, 16):\n    for T in nx.nonisomorphic_trees(n):\n        rad = nx.radius(T)\n        if rad >= 4:\n            r = rdn(T)\n            if rad + 1 > r:\n                print('COUNTEREXAMPLE!', n, rad, r)\n            elif rad + 1 == r:\n                print(f'TIGHT TREE: n={n}, rad={rad}, rdn={r}')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Run ILP on trees","toolSummary":"Check tight trees rad >= 4"}}]}
{"step_index":1690,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:01:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T02:01:26+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: d3e5d288-f78f-46c8-8e31-a1a54e2a343d/task-1690\nTask Description: /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport pulp\n\ndef rdn(G):\n    prob = pulp.LpProblem('RDN', pulp.LpMinimize)\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    x = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'x_{v}', cat='Binary') for v in nodes}\n    y = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'y_{v}', cat='Binary') for v in nodes}\n    prob += pulp.lpSum([x[v] + 2*y[v] for v in nodes])\n    for v in nodes:\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] <= 1\n        # v dominated: either x[v]==1, y[v]==1, or neighbor has y[u]==1\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] + pulp.lpSum([y[u] for u in G.neighbors(v)]) >= 1\n    prob.solve(pulp.PULP_CBC_CMD(msg=0))\n    return int(round(pulp.value(prob.objective)))\n\n# Check all trees up to n=15\nimport itertools\n\nfor n in range(8, 16):\n    for T in nx.nonisomorphic_trees(n):\n        rad = nx.radius(T)\n        if rad >= 4:\n            r = rdn(T)\n            if rad + 1 > r:\n                print('COUNTEREXAMPLE!', n, rad, r)\n            elif rad + 1 == r:\n                print(f'TIGHT TREE: n={n}, rad={rad}, rdn={r}')\n\"\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d3e5d288-f78f-46c8-8e31-a1a54e2a343d/.system_generated/tasks/task-1690.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
