{"step_index":1707,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:01:52Z","thinking":"**Addressing Axiom Rejection**\n\nThe auditor detected that the completion utilizes problematic axioms like `sorryAx`. This means the current proof attempt will be rejected. The focus must shift to crafting a proof without these axioms, or finding a refutation.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman Domination Proof**\n\nExamining the relationship between the radius and Roman domination number. The initial conjecture that radius(G) + 1 <= romanDominationNumber(G) is being tested. Deductions suggest this implies radius(G) + 1 <= romanWeight(f) for all Roman dominating functions.\n\nIf this inequality holds for the Roman domination number, it must be true for all Roman dominating functions due to the minimization definition. Verifying this, if  romanWeight(f) >=  radius(G) + 1 is true for a given Roman dominating function f and if the conjecture holds, then the minimum is also above the radius + 1.\n\nThe goal is now to use the given facts from `prove_e20263a9`, namely that $G$ is connected and nontrivial, to form a proof.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":true,"Includes":["*.lean"],"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"def radius","SearchPath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing","toolAction":"Search for def radius in repo","toolSummary":"Search for def radius"}}]}
